{
  "info": {
    "name": "StyleHub API Testing",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "IMPORT: Postman > Import > select this JSON. No export is needed. Start FastAPI at http://127.0.0.1:8000. Use the desktop app or desktop agent for localhost. Do not select an environment overriding these variables.\nRUN: Run only folder 01 - Core API checks in order, one iteration. It creates a fresh test account automatically; you do not need to enter your personal password. Requires seeded products and one product with >=3 stock. Creates then cancels a test order and restores stock. Do not run alongside other stock-changing tests. Check Test Results for actual results; this file is not evidence of completed testing.\nOPTIONAL PAYMENTS: After Core, manually send P1-P4 in folder 02. This reserves one unit and creates an unpaid Stripe test PaymentIntent. Keep stripe listen --events payment_intent.succeeded,payment_intent.payment_failed,payment_intent.canceled --forward-to http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/payments/webhook running with its signing secret configured in backend .env. Use stripe payment_intents confirm YOUR_PI_ID --payment-method=pm_card_visa for success, or --payment-method=pm_card_chargeDeclined for failure, then retry visa on the same intent. Alternatively stripe payment_intents cancel YOUR_PI_ID releases stock via webhook. Send P5 after the event to inspect order state. Do not leave a pending reservation unintentionally. No Stripe secret is stored in this file.\nSHARE: Downloaded original JSON has no personal credentials/tokens. Runtime-generated test credentials and token stay in Postman. Keep the original file for GitHub submission; do not share screenshots of tokens or client_secret. Backend user-isolation and frontend checks are separate from this collection."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "product_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "size",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "unit_price_paise",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "stock_before",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "cart_item_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "checkout_key",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "order_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "payment_checkout_key",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "payment_intent_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Core API checks (run this folder)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/",
            "description": "",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"API healthy\",()=>pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.equal(\"ok\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "02 Register fresh test user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/register",
            "description": "",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Demo\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const id=pm.variables.replaceIn(\"{{$guid}}\");",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"email\", \"stylehub-\"+id+\"@example.com\");",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"password\", \"Demo9!\"+id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.unset(\"access_token\");",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.unset(\"order_id\");",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.unset(\"cart_item_id\");"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if(pm.response.code===201){pm.collectionVariables.set(\"user_id\",pm.response.json().id);pm.test(\"Hash excluded\",()=>pm.expect(pm.response.json()).not.to.have.property(\"hashed_password\"));}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
